{
    "frames": {
        "study-intro": {
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "emph": true,
                    "text": "Important: your child does not need to be with you until the test trials begin. First, let's go over what will happen.",
                    "title": "Listen for the babbles or giggles!"
                },
                {
                    "text": "In this study:",
                    "listblocks": [
                        {
                            "text": "We'll set up your webcam and record your consent to participate."
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "You'll answer several questions about your child's development."
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Then, we'll make sure your audio and video is working and teach you how to hold your baby in front of the camera."
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Afterwards, your baby will hear several short audio recordings of adults and infants."
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "text": "First, let's get your webcam set up."
                },
                {
                    "text": "Please click 'Next' to proceed."
                }
            ],
            "showPreviousButton": false,
            "kind": "exp-lookit-text"
        },
        "video-config": {
            "kind": "exp-video-config",
            "troubleshootingIntro": "If you're having any trouble getting your webcam set up, please feel free to email the Infant Learning Project lab at infantlearningproject@utdallas.edu and we would be glad to help you out!"
        },
        "video-consent": {
            "kind": "exp-lookit-video-consent",
            "template": "consent_001",
            "PIName": "Melanie J. Spence",
            "institution": "The University of Texas at Dallas",
            "PIContact": "Melanie J. Spence at mspence@utdallas.edu",
            "purpose": "The purpose of this study is to better understand the types of sounds and speakers that young infants are more likely to attend to. In this study, your infant will hear different types of sounds and we will measure how long your infant looks and pays attention to them. Infants’ interest and attention to these vocalizations may help us understand how infants at different ages are developing language and social connections.",
            "procedures": "You will register for the study and complete several short questionnaires focused on information about you and your baby. Then, the main part of the study will begin; it will last less than 5 minutes. Before we begin this part of the study, we ask that you position your chair so that your back is facing the computer screen and you will hold your baby to your chest so that your baby can see the computer screen over your shoulder. Your baby will then listen to a series of short audios. During the study, your baby will first be shown a colorful image to attract attention to the computer screen. Then your baby will be presented with a series of short audio recordings of adult and infant sounds paired with an image. Some babies will hear recordings of speech, and some babies will hear recordings of laughter. A tone will sound when the study is finished and you may turn back around to face the computer.",
            "payment": "After you finish the study, you will have the opportunity to download a certificate of participation. To be eligible to receive this certificate, your child must be in the age range specified for this study, you must submit a valid consent statement, and we must be able to confirm that there is a child with you. However, you may download a certificate even if you don't finish the study, or if we are not able to use your child's data. There are no other direct benefits to you or your child associated with participating in this study, but we hope that you enjoy the experience. There are no anticipated risks associated with participating.",
            "datause": "We are primarily interested in your child's eye movements in response to the video stimuli. A research assistant will watch your video to measure the amount of time your baby spends looking at the screen.",
            "gdpr": false,
            "research_rights_statement": "You are not waiving any legal claims, rights or remedies because of your participation in this research study. If you feel you have been treated unfairly, or you have questions regarding your rights as a research subject, you may contact the Office of Research at The University of Texas at Dallas, 972-883-4570, research@utdallas.edu.",
            "addtional_segments": [
                {
                    "title": "US Patriot Act Disclosure",
                    "text": "Lookit is a U.S. organization and all information gathered from the website is stored on servers based in the U.S. Therefore, your video recordings are subject to U.S. laws, such as the US Patriot Act. This act allows authorities access to the records of internet service providers. If you choose to participate in this study, you understand that your video recording will be stored and accessed in the USA. The security and privacy policy for Lookit can be found at the follwing link: <a href='https://lookit.mit.edu/privacy/'target='_blank'>https://lookit.mit.edu/privacy/</a>. "
                }
            ]
        },
        "questionnaire-instructions": {
            "blocks": [
                {
                    "title": "Questionnaires"
                },
                {
                    "text": "Now you will complete three questionnaires so we can learn a little bit more about your baby and understand whether more experience making certain sounds (like babbles or laughter) influence the sounds infants prefer to listen to. The answers to these surveys will not affect your ability to participate in the study, so please answer honestly."
                },
                {
                    "text": "<strong>The Development Survey</strong> will ask you about demographic information such as what language you speak at home."
                },
                {
                    "text": "<strong>The Language Survey</strong> will ask about your baby's language abilities based on their age."
                },
                {
                    "text": "<strong>The Humor Survey</strong> will ask about when your babys started to laugh and what types of things they laugh at. "
                },
                {
                    "text": "After the questionnaires, you will recieve instructions to prepare for the study."
                },
                {
                    "text": "Please click 'Next' to proceed."
                }
            ],
            "showPreviousButton": false,
            "kind": "exp-lookit-text"
        },
