            "blocks": [
                {
                    "title": "Study Overview",
                    "listblocks": [
                        {
                            "text": "Your baby will hear 12 10-second recordings. Half of the babies in this study will be listening to recordings of speech sounds, and half of the babies will be listening to recordings of laughter. Which videos your baby will be viewing is determined at random. We want to see how the babies react!"
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The audios in the study are quite repetitive and short so they might start to sound strange to your adult ears! We are trying to learn about the very small building blocks of language and how your baby reacts to them."
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "You will also hear a chime noise multiple times during the study. This accompanies a video of a small colorful ball in the center of the screen. The purpose for this extra video is to keep your child's attention throughout the study. There will be a chime sound at the beginning and the end of the test trials."
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "The trials will take about 3 minutes to complete. After that, you will be able to select a level of privacy for your data."
                        },
                        {
                            "text": "Let's make sure your audio and video are working, then teach you how to hold your baby in front of the camera before we begin the study."
                        }
                    ]
                },
